ERRORS BY CATEGORY
==================

1. MISSING HEADERS / UNDECLARED IDENTIFIERS
--------------------------------------------
- src/engine/math_util.c:830 — FLT_EPSILON undeclared
  Missing #include <float.h>
  FIX: Added #include <float.h> to math_util.c

2. MACRO PREPROCESSOR ISSUES (EM_ASM commas)
---------------------------------------------
- src/pc/audio/audio_web.h:44,59 — EM_ASM({...}) fails because
  commas in JavaScript code (array literals, for-loop arguments)
  are interpreted as macro argument separators by the C preprocessor.
  EM_ASM only tracks parentheses, not braces, for argument matching.
  FIX: Replaced EM_ASM({...}) with emscripten_run_script() and
  emscripten_run_script_int() using string concatenation.

3. STRUCT MEMBER / PTHREAD ERRORS (ThreadHandle.mutex)
-------------------------------------------------------
- src/pc/mods/mod_cache.c:256 — pthread_mutex_lock undeclared, no 'mutex' member
- src/pc/mods/mods.c:214,244,256,263,267 — same
- data/dynos_gfx_init.cpp:37,61,80 — same
  Root cause: LOADING_SCREEN_MUTEX macro in src/pc/loading.h directly
  calls pthread_mutex_lock/unlock and accesses .mutex member, but the
  TARGET_WEB ThreadHandle struct (in thread.h) has no mutex field.
  FIX: Added #ifdef TARGET_WEB branch in loading.h macro that executes
  the protected code without mutex (single-threaded on web).

4. MISSING GENERATED FILES (level entry symbols + textures)
------------------------------------------------------------
- levels/level_defines.h:23+ — level_bbh_entry, level_ccm_entry, etc. undeclared
  Root cause: build/us_web/include/level_headers.h was empty because
  emcc's preprocessor (-E -P) doesn't recognize .h.in extension.
  FIX: Added -x c flag to CPP definition in Makefile.web so emcc
  treats .h.in files as C source for preprocessing.

- levels/castle_courtyard/texture.inc.c:2 — 0_custom.rgba16.inc.c not found
- levels/castle_grounds/texture.inc.c:12 — 6_custom.rgba16.inc.c not found
  Root cause: Texture .inc.c generation depends on .d dependency files
  from prior builds. On first clean build, make doesn't know these
  dependencies exist. This is a pre-existing issue not specific to web.
  Expected to resolve on subsequent builds once .d files are populated.

5. BUILD SYSTEM ISSUES (fixed before first compilation)
--------------------------------------------------------
- tangle Makefile.web — GNU Make's built-in suffix rule for .web->.p
  tried to process Makefile.web as a CWEB literate programming file.
  FIX: Added --no-builtin-rules to inner make invocation.

- build/us_web/src/engine/behavior_script.d: No such file or directory
  GNU Make 3.81 (macOS default) doesn't support the != operator for
  shell execution during Makefile parsing. The DUMMY != mkdir -p
  line silently failed.
  FIX: Switched to gmake (GNU Make 4.4.1 via brew install make).

